{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429258-second-edition-character-creation","id":429258,"title":"Second Edition Character Creation!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-05T13:55:31-08:00","id":429258,"title":"Second Edition Character Creation!","content":"First of all, to the writers of second edition, you beautiful bastards. Really, thank you.<br /> <br /> <br /> So anyways, I'm bored and unable to run a Second Edition game, so I'm going to do some character creation, and share some of my thoughts. Feel free to contribute you own character concepts.<br /> <hr /><br /> <div align=\"center\"><b>Conaron Hill Pack</b><br /> </div> This pack has barely started, it based around a disused car-garage in the Conaron Hill district of the local city. It only has three Uratha members, one Wolf-Blooded and a few mortals 'in the know'. First the werewolves:<br /> <hr /><br /> <div align=\"center\"><b>Richard Keel</b><br /> </div> Blood: The Destoyer Bone: Lone Wolf<br /> Concept: Territorial Defender<br /> Auspice: Itheaur Tribe: Hunters in Darkness<br /> <br /> Intelligence: 3 Strength: 2 Presence: 1<br /> Wits: 2 Dexterity: 3 Manipulation: 2<br /> Resolve: 3 Stamina: 2 Composure: 3<br /> <br /> Crafts: 2, <b>Investigation</b>: 2, Medicine (First Aid): 1, <b>Occult</b>: 3<br /> Athletics: 2, Brawl (Urhan): 3, Larceny: 1, Stealth (Shadowing): 3, Survival:2<br /> Intimidation: 2, Streetwise: 2<br /> <br /> Safe Place (shared): 2, Totem (shared): 1, Favoured Form (Urhan): 2, Professional Training (Occultist): 2, Anonymity: 2<br /> <br /> Renown: Purity: 2, Wisdom: 1<br /> <br /> Aspirations<br /> Kill an interloper (s)<br /> Build a den (l)<br /> Hunt a shartha (s)<br /> <br /> Triggers: Passive (Territory), Common (Wound), Specific (Pack)<br /> Touchstones: The Old Gang, The Lune<br /> <br /> Gifts<br /> Crescent 1<br /> Nature (Glory) Black Earth Red Hunger, Ward (Glory) Predator's Claim<br /> Pack (Wisdom) Pack Awareness<br /> <br /> Rites<br /> Rite of the Sacred Hunt<br /> <br /> <i>So a nice Hunters template, all th new stuff really helps build a space for the character to inhabit. The Touchstones immediately give me (the ST) some NPCs to have fun with. I'll probably say this time and time again, but I do like the new Gifts. Keel is an occult focussed character, with little social skills and penchant for punishing breaches of territory, he seems to be the driver of the packs vengeance. God help their enemies when he realises more of his Crescent Moon potential.</i> <div align=\"center\"> <hr /><br /> <br /> <b>Anna Redick</b></div> Blood: The Challenger Bone: Guru<br /> Concept: Changed Historian<br /> Auspice: Cahalith Tribe: Bone Shadow<br /> <br /> Intelligence: 2 Strength: 2 Presence: 3<br /> Wits: 3 Dexterity: 2 Manipulation: 3<br /> Resolve: 3 Stamina: 2 Composure: 2<br /> <br /> Academics (History): 2, Crafts: 2, Investigation: 2, Occult: 1, Politics: 1<br /> Athletics: 1, Brawl (Dalu): 2, Survival: 1<br /> Animal Ken: 1, Empathy: 2, Expression (Guitars): 3, Intimidation 1, Persuasion: 2, Socialise: 2, Streetwise: 1<br /> <br /> Professional Training (Historian): 1, Hearing Whispers: 2, Safe Place (shared): 1, Totem (shared): 1, Allies (Spirit Court): 1, Barfly: 1, Mentor 1: Resources: 1, Striking Looks: 1<br /> <br /> Renown: Glory: 1, Wisdom 1, Cunning 1<br /> <br /> Aspirations<br /> Play a gig (s)<br /> Fall into Kuruth (s)<br /> Join a Lodge (l)<br /> <br /> Touchstones<br /> The Ex, The Buddy Spirit<br /> <br /> Triggers<br /> Passive (Moon), Common (Blood), Specific (Pack)<br /> <br /> Gifts<br /> Gibbous 1<br /> Death (Glory) Barghest, Knowledge (Wisdom) Sifting the Sands<br /> Hunting (Cunning) Honed Senses<br /> <br /> Rites<br /> Messenger<br /> Banish<br /> <br /> <i>Also fun. More of an intellectual Cahalith powers wise, though she has a good basis in social skills. The thing that strikes out to me now is that, unsurprisingly, the first dot Moon Gifts are just plain useful, not matter what Auspice your character has, they'll find some use out of Auspice 1 dot. Anna strikes me as the waypoint of the pack, more collected. She would work well providing the information for the others to use. Then blast the packs enemies with her War Howl.</i><br /> <hr /> <div align=\"center\"><b>John Dunne</b></div> <br /> Blood: The Soldier Bone: Community Organisation<br /> Concept: Flock Waren<br /> Auspice: Rahu Tribes: Iron Master<br /> <br /> Intelligence: 2 Strength: 3 Presence: 3<br /> Wits: 2 Dexterity: 2 Manipulation: 2<br /> Resolve: 2 Stamina: 3 Composure: 2<br /> <br /> Investigation (Crime): 2, Medicine: 1, Politics (Police): 1<br /> Athletics: 2, Brawl: 3, Drive: 1, <b>Firearms</b>: 2, Larceny: 1, Survival: 2, Weaponry: 1<br /> Empathy (Emotions): 1, Intimidation: 1, Persuasion: 2, <b>Streetwise: </b>2, Subterfuge: 1<br /> <br /> Professional Training (Police): 2, Trained Observer: 1, Safe Place (shared): 1, Totem (shared): 1, Resources: 1, Residential Area: 2, Sounds of the City: 2<br /> <br /> Renown<br /> Purity: 2, Cunning: 1<br /> <br /> Aspirations<br /> Leave the Police (s)<br /> Find the Serial Killer (l)<br /> Gain Uratha respect (s)<br /> <br /> Touchstones<br /> The Parents, The Future Self<br /> <br /> Triggers<br /> Passive (Moon), Common (Pack), Specific (The Other)<br /> <br /> Gifts<br /> Full Moon 1<br /> Dominance (Purity): Snarl of the Predator, Knowledge (Purity): Lore of the Land, Strength (Cunning): Unchained<br /> <br /> Rites<br /> Rite of the Sacred Hunt<br /> <br /> <i>So here's the face of the pack with regards to mortals, even though he's a Rahu, god help them. Looking at the various Gifts Rahu can get, it would be fun playing this ex-copper as he becomes a shredder. Again, the Touchstones are giving the ST two NPCs per PCs. It is rather good. Also, the Community Merit is an awesome little goodness.</i><br /> <hr /><br /> <b>Others</b><br /> <br /> So the rest of the pack, as you'll note they don't have a locus. This pack instead uses a Wolf-Blooded with <i>that</i> tell. Mortal members are members of the local community, with some specialisations. There's the &quot;I know a guy&quot;, there's the &quot;I was a surgeon <i>dammit</i>&quot; and then there's the kid who's cycling around and is always watching.<br /> <br /> The pack creation is really cool. I'm going to look forward to running that at some point. ^_^<br /> <br /> The Totem? Well it's getting late. I'll post that later, with an Idigam.<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> So, who are your guys and gals? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/417-the_duck","name":"the_duck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T18:59:17-08:00","id":429616,"title":"","content":"Richard can't have the glory facets in either one of his two shadow gifts, no dots in glory","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/991-pgolasze13","name":"pgolasze13","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}